.Dd November 15, 2026
.Dt WLCLIENT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm wlclient
.Nd Wayland test client and end-to-end check
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar seconds Op Cm panel | Cm workspace
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility is a small Wayland client.
It checks that the Wayland stack works from end to end:
the connection to the compositor, shared-memory buffers passed as file
descriptors, the keymap, and the shell protocols.
It is meant to be run against
.Xr wlcompd 8 .
.Pp
.Nm
connects to the compositor, lists the globals it offers, and then runs
one of three tests.
It reports each step on standard output.
.Pp
The
.Ar seconds
argument is a whole number of seconds.
If it is missing or zero, the default test exits as soon as it is done.
To give a mode, a
.Ar seconds
value must come first.
An unknown mode runs the default test.
.Ss Default test
.Nm
opens a toplevel window titled
.Dq wlclient
and waits to be configured.
It then draws a test pattern into a shared-memory buffer and commits it.
The pattern is an orange border with a white diagonal on a blue field.
.Nm
prints a checksum of the pixels in each frame.
.Xr wlcompd 8
prints the checksum of what it received, so the two can be compared.
.Pp
.Nm
also binds a keyboard and checks that the keymap it is sent is XKB text.
It adds a 64 by 48 subsurface at offset 24,24, a 120 by 80 popup, and a
16 by 16 green cursor that it sets when the pointer enters its surface.
.Pp
If
.Ar seconds
is greater than zero,
.Nm
then stays connected for that long.
When the compositor asks for a new size,
.Nm
draws a new frame at that size, growing its shared-memory pool if needed.
Key events are printed as they arrive.
.Ss Panel test
With
.Cm panel ,
.Nm
creates a layer-shell surface in the top layer, named
.Dq wlpanel .
It is anchored to the left, right and bottom edges, 28 pixels high, with
an exclusive zone of 28 pixels.
.Nm
waits to be configured, fills the surface with a single colour, and stays
for
.Ar seconds
seconds, or 5 seconds if
.Ar seconds
is zero.
The test passes if the compositor gives the panel a width and a height of
28 pixels.
.Ss Workspace test
With
.Cm workspace ,
.Nm
first runs the default test up to the popup.
It then lists the virtual desktops offered through ext-workspace,
switches to desktop 1, waits a second, switches back to desktop 0 and
waits another second.
The test passes if there are exactly four desktops and desktop 0 is
active at the end.
.Ar seconds
is ignored in this mode.
.Pp
Each test ends by printing
.Dq ALL PASS
or a failure message.
If the compositor asks
.Nm
to close its window or its panel, it exits at once.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
.It Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
The directory that holds the compositor's socket.
.It Ev WAYLAND_DISPLAY
The name of the socket in that directory.
The default is
.Pa wayland-0 .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 if the test passed, and 1 otherwise.
.Pp
The default test passes if a frame was drawn and, when a keyboard is
available, a valid keymap was received.
.Nm
also exits 1 if it cannot connect, if a required global is missing, or
if it is never configured.
If the compositor asks it to close,
.Nm
exits 0.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Check the stack, then serve resizes for 30 seconds:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wlclient 30
.Ed
.Pp
Check that a panel docks to the bottom edge:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wlclient 10 panel
.Ed
.Pp
Check virtual desktop switching:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wlclient 0 workspace
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr wlcoreprobe 1 ,
.Xr wlprobe 1 ,
.Xr shm_open 3 ,
.Xr fbcompd 8 ,
.Xr wlcompd 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in Ixolo 0.1.
.Sh BUGS
In the default test,
.Nm
waits for events from the compositor.
If none arrive, it can stay running past
.Ar seconds .
.Pp
The workspace test does not check that the switch to desktop 1 took
effect.
.Pp
Whether the compositor released the buffer is printed but does not
change the exit status.
